The GCC gate is blocked because the local GCC 9.4 can't compile this Jolt revision (it lacks `__builtin_bit_cast`), and no GCC 11 is installed. Closing it needs a GCC 11+ environment. I haven't checked the CI GCC 11 job, so the GCC result is unverified in both places.

**Build decisions you may want to review**
- Jolt's target builds as C++20 and with SSE4.2, and the same macros are exported to consumers. Its vendor policy is unchanged, so it has no `-Werror`.
- Clang 10 needed three local workarounds, all in `engine/physics/CMakeLists.txt`: C++20 for Jolt, no precompiled header on Jolt, and `-g1` in Debug. Clang 11+ and MSVC keep the upstream settings.
- Shapes are box and sphere only. Colliders, filters, and queries belong to US-053.
- The adapter subscribes to the large-world origin. The acceptance criteria don't require it, but without it the float positions would go stale after a rebase.
- `worker_threads` defaults to 1, and the catch-up cap defaults to 4 steps.

**Status:** US-052 is **Partial**. I did not emit the completion signal, because the GCC gate and the benchmark are open.
